@X0BControl Panel
-------------
@X03The Control panel is a program which is designed to launch multiple pcboard
nodes with minimal batch files involved, and gives you additional control over
the status of your nodes, as well as displaying the status, user, and user
location for each node.

The filename for Control Panel is PCBCP.EXE.  This filename should have a
read-only attribute assigned to it, and should be located in the \PCB
directory.

A few things that are necessary for all OS/2 installations of PCBoard (dos
or OS/2).

@X091) In your CONFIG.SYS file, edit the line that says:
   @X07SET PATH=
   @X09Append to the end:
   @X07C:\PCB;
   @X09Make sure that all paths are separated by a semicolon (;).
 
2) In your AUTOEXEC.BAT file, edit the line that says:
   @X07PATH=
   @X09Append to the end:
   @X07C:\PCB;
   @X09Make sure that all paths are separated by a semicolon (;).

If your PCBoard installation is on a drive other than C:, then substitute that
drive letter in the paths specified in steps 1 and 2 above.

@X03As stated in bulletin #1, don't assume anything.  DOUBLE check these lines.
If you have any trouble with any pcboard function that involves shells, then
it's likely that this is the reason.

@X0AThe steps outlined above apply to either the dos version OR the OS/2 version.

